{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The elders of Midian</b> — Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said that it is possible that the five kings were elders, and if so, \"the elders of Moab and the elders of Midian went\" (Numbers 22:7) are not the elders mentioned at the beginning, for the kings did not go before him; only officers did, as written (Numbers 22:8). And according to the opinion of our Sages (Numbers Rabbah 20:4), who said: their leader in Midian was raised there — it is fitting for them to send to the elders of Midian, neither to the kings nor to the people, for the elders are the ones who know the matter. \n\nAnd what appears correct in my eyes is that at first there were kings in Midian. And Sihon king of the Amorites waged war against the first king of Moab, and took all his land from his hand as far as the Arnon. And he waged war against the children of Ammon and took from their land, as the king of Ammon said to Jephthah: \"because Israel took my land when he came up from Egypt\" (Judges 11:13), and Jephthah answered him that from Sihon Israel had taken it (there, verse 21). And it is written in Joshua (13:25): \"And their territory was Jazer and all the cities of Gilead and half the land of the children of Ammon as far as Aroer.\" And Sihon further waged war against the kings of Midian and conquered their land, and made them servants to himself bearing tribute, and removed the crown of their heads and did not grant them the dignity of kingship, but left them as judges in the land of Midian on his behalf. And therefore they are called \"the elders of Midian,\" after the manner of \"the gate to the elders\" (Deuteronomy 25:7). \n\nAnd the proof for this is what is written in Joshua (13:21): \"And all the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorite, who reigned in Heshbon, whom Moses struck — him and the princes of Midian, Evi and Rekem and Zur and Hur and Reba, the princes of Sihon, inhabitants of the land\" — for they were under his dominion. And the reason for \"and the kings of Midian\" (Numbers 31:8) is that they had been kings at first, as he said, \"the princes of Midian, the princes of Sihon.\" And so too it is stated: \"head of the ancestral house in Midian was he\" (Numbers 25:15) — not \"king.\" Or the reason for \"kings of Midian\" may be that they had returned to their kingship at that time. \n\nAnd I do not know the reason why Scripture says, \"Balak son of Zippor was king for Moab at that time,\" for it would be fitting for it to say first, \"Balak son of Zippor, king of Moab, saw all that Israel had done to the Amorite.\" Perhaps Balak was a mighty warrior, renowned greatly for his might and valor, and Scripture mentioned that even though Moab had at that time a powerful king, mighty of heart among warriors, he was afraid and greatly distressed because of the children of Israel. Therefore Jephthah said: \"Are you any better than Balak son of Zippor, king of Moab?\" (Judges 11:25) — for one does not intimidate a king except with a very fearsome king. \n\nAnd it is possible that Moab had no king over them, and the people were greatly afraid because of the children of Israel, and they did two things: they sent to the elders of Midian, saying, \"Now the congregation will lick up,\" and they set up this king over themselves at the counsel of Midian, and afterward they all sent to Balaam at the king's command. And this is the reason for <b>at that time</b> — when they took counsel concerning the matter of Israel and sent them to Balaam. And the reason for <b>and Balak saw</b> would be that he was one of the officers of Moab and a mighty warrior, and he stirred himself up concerning this matter and said to Moab, \"Come, let us deal wisely with the people,\" and they arose and crowned him at the counsel of Midian. \n\nAnd in the midrash of Numbers Rabbah (Numbers Rabbah 20:4) I found: \"Balak son of Zippor was king for Moab at that time\" — but was he not at first a prince, as stated, \"Evi and Rekem and Zur and Hur and Reba\"? Rather, once Sihon was killed, they crowned him over them — \"at that time,\" for the hour brought it about for him."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:54.262672904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}